@{ViewData["Title"]="Privacy notice — draft";}
<h1>Privacy notice — draft</h1><p>Version preview-2026-10-10. Not finalized for live intake. Operator identity, hosting arrangements, relevant markets, lawful bases and rights procedures need review before launch. Contact: <a href="mailto:contact.stay@funtoolie.com">contact.stay@funtoolie.com</a>; delivery and monitoring are not yet verified.</p>
<p>StayWidget uses common Funtoolio Google sign-in for owners. It keeps an issuer/subject identity and display name; it does not access Gmail. Secure service cookies are used for owner login and antiforgery. Guests do not need an account or cookies.</p>
<p>Reservation requests collect name, phone, dates, unit and guest count. Guests should not submit passport data, payment details or sensitive free text. Property owners determine their booking use; the service's controller/processor responsibilities and agreements must be assessed for the actual operator and market.</p>
<p>Private links are bearer capabilities. Anyone with a complete link can use its scoped permissions. They expire, can be revoked, and are removed from retry recovery after 24 hours. Authorized owner management/export still contains guest data and must be handled privately.</p>
<p>Provisional retention: closed unaccepted enquiry contacts 90 days; booking contacts 12 months after departure/cancellation; nonpersonal history 24 months; activity 12 months. Upcoming bookings are preserved. Feedback is private: closed or unreviewed New records expire after 12 months, selected ongoing work remains until closed. Product account deletion is a coordinated operator procedure; common-auth deletion is separate. Backup expiry and deletion reapplication must be established before production.</p>
<p>No tracking scripts, visitor identifiers, advertising profiles or third-party analytics are included. Optional first-party daily counters count fixed public page requests, widget responses, committed requests, installation acknowledgements and attribution clicks. They are approximate counts, not unique visitors. No tenant, guest, token, IP or referrer is stored in them. They are disabled by default; DNT: 1 and Sec-GPC: 1 opt out when enabled. Raw networks are transiently used in abuse controls as process-local keyed hashes. Metrics expire after 90 days and failures do not affect bookings.</p>
<p>Routine feedback is not the security/privacy rights channel. Use the contact address above for rights or security reports; never send a private guest link or password. Identity verification, applicable response obligations, incident handling and any international transfer requirements need review. This draft does not establish legal compliance.</p>
